  "lines": [
    {"page": 1, "start": 0, "end": 100, "top": 72.0, "left": 72.0, "lastX": 516.0, "baseline": 82.58, "inkLeft": 72.024, "text": "The morning ferry crosses the estuary twice before the tide turns, carrying commuters, bicycles and "},
    {"page": 1, "start": 100, "end": 205, "top": 85.2, "left": 72.0, "lastX": 538.2, "baseline": 96.02, "inkLeft": 72.024, "text": "crates of vegetables from the farms on the far shore. Nobody on board hurries; they read, drink tea from "},
    {"page": 1, "start": 205, "end": 308, "top": 99.0, "left": 72.0, "lastX": 532.8, "baseline": 109.46, "inkLeft": 72.024, "text": "flasks and watch the herons stand in the shallows. When the ferry docks, a short queue forms along the "},
    {"page": 1, "start": 308, "end": 367, "top": 112.2, "left": 72.0, "lastX": 329.4, "baseline": 122.93, "inkLeft": 72.024, "text": "jetty and the deckhand coils the rope with practised ease.\u000d"},
    {"page": 1, "start": 367, "end": 470, "top": 132.0, "left": 72.0, "lastX": 540.0, "baseline": 142.37, "inkLeft": 72.024, "text": "A well-made map leaves out far more than it shows. The cartographer decides which roads matter, which "},
    {"page": 1, "start": 470, "end": 575, "top": 145.2, "left": 72.0, "lastX": 526.8, "baseline": 155.81, "inkLeft": 72.024, "text": "rivers deserve a name and where a label may sit without hiding a village. Every choice trades detail for "},
    {"page": 1, "start": 575, "end": 677, "top": 159.0, "left": 72.0, "lastX": 522.6, "baseline": 169.25, "inkLeft": 72.024, "text": "clarity, and the reader trusts the result because the trades were made carefully and applied the same "},
    {"page": 1, "start": 677, "end": 705, "top": 172.2, "left": 72.0, "lastX": 197.4, "baseline": 182.69, "inkLeft": 72.024, "text": "way across the whole sheet.\u000d"},
    {"page": 1, "start": 705, "end": 815, "top": 191.4, "left": 72.0, "lastX": 539.4, "baseline": 202.15, "inkLeft": 72.024, "text": "In the workshop the lamps stay lit late. Shavings gather under the bench, a kettle ticks as it cools, and the "},
    {"page": 1, "start": 815, "end": 923, "top": 204.6, "left": 72.0, "lastX": 523.2, "baseline": 215.35, "inkLeft": 72.024, "text": "half-finished chair waits for its last joint. The maker steps back, squints along the rail and decides that "},
    {"page": 1, "start": 923, "end": 1026, "top": 218.4, "left": 72.0, "lastX": 527.4, "baseline": 228.79, "inkLeft": 72.024, "text": "tomorrow will do for the glue, since good work is not improved by being rushed past the point of care.\u000d"},
    {"page": 2, "start": 1026, "end": 1104, "top": 72.0, "left": 181.8, "lastX": 513.0, "baseline": 82.58, "inkLeft": 181.51, "text": "The morning ferry crosses the estuary twice before the tide turns, carrying "},
    {"page": 2, "start": 1104, "end": 1182, "top": 85.2, "left": 181.8, "lastX": 528.6, "baseline": 96.02, "inkLeft": 181.51, "text": "commuters, bicycles and crates of vegetables from the farms on the far shore. "},
